Body part module:
```
module body_part(i) {
  front = 0;
  // B socket ring at front, body local x R_SEP..L-R_SEP
  difference() {
    union() {
      // ring outer disk
      translate([0,0,0]) cylinder(h=T, r=R_RING);
      // neck
      linear_extrude(T) neck_2d();
      // main body 2D
      linear_extrude(T) body_2d(i);
      // rear pin (if i<5)
      if (i<5) translate([L,0,0]) pin_solid();
      // rear arm
      if (i<5) linear_extrude(T) arm_2d(...);
    }
    // socket cavity (subtract full height)
    socket_cavity();
    // mouth cut
    mouth_cut();
  }
}
```
Need subtract socket cavity only at front. `socket_cavity()` itself at origin. This will also cut body material if overlapping; intended.
Order: subtract cavity and mouth from union. But if body_2d extends left of x8? For tail maybe no. Body rect x8..18. Neck x6.5..10; mouth cut on left won't hit neck. Good.
For body5 tail body_2d from x8 to26. union ring/neck. subtract cavity/mouth. No rear pin/arm.
For body i=1..4, body_2d x8..18; arm to L; pin at L. The arm/pin should not be cut by front cavity/mouth (far). Fine.

But B ring at front plus body/neck: the body may be too far right; ring connected by neck. When `difference` subtracts socket cavity, it also subtracts a cylindrical volume r5.5 bottom/top etc from neck if neck overlaps x6.5,y0 (r6.5 >5.5, not cut) and body x8. Good.

Mouth wedge cut extends through z; it may cut neck? wedge x<0 only, no.

`body_2d(i)`: if i<5 rounded rect x R_SEP..L-R_SEP (8..18), y±BODY_W/2=9. For body5 tail polygon. Need union with `neck` x=6.5..10 y±3.
Rounded body rect via hull of 4 circles radius2 at (10,±7),(16,±7) gives x8..18 y±9. For i<5.
Tail polygon maybe start x8,-9 to16,-9,22,-5,26,0,22,5,16,9,8,9. Could round using offset but okay. Maybe body5 tail shape should start x8 to16 full width then taper. Use polygon with vertex at (26,0). Since union with neck. At x8,y±9 abrupt vertical edge; body front at x8, ring gap .5. That's fine. For aesthetics, body5 could have rounded corners; not critical.

Tail end at x=L=26, pointed. Overall x = front132+26=158.

